// Example 02: named types.
//
// The rule behind Jadpo's types: representation is not meaning. A weight
// and a temperature are both whole numbers underneath, but they mean
// different things, so they are different types, and the compiler never
// converts between them silently. A value becomes a type only by being
// checked against that type's rules.
//
// This project is a bakery's pantry. Each action shows one family of
// built-in types:
//
//   domains/pantry/types/grams.jadpo            a type two files share
//   domains/pantry/actions/weigh_flour.jadpo    whole numbers, Bool, conversions
//   domains/pantry/actions/price_flour.jadpo    exact decimals and their scale
//   domains/pantry/actions/label_jar.jadpo      text: lengths, patterns, refinements
//   domains/pantry/actions/check_delivery.jadpo identities, emails, links, time
//
// Read them in that order; each has a test file beside it.
application {}
